= Knowledge representation — Simple =

'''Knowledge representation''' is how we write knowledge in a structured form so a computer can use and reason with it.

For example, instead of storing only a paragraph saying:

> Mars is a planet.

a knowledge system might store:

<pre>
Mars → is a → Planet
</pre>

It can also store relations such as:

<pre>
Mars → orbits → Sun
</pre>

The representation is not the real world. It is a model of part of the world.

Different representation systems use:
* rules;
* logic;
* graphs;
* ontologies;
* probabilities.

The way knowledge is represented changes what a computer can easily infer.

